## Deployment

### Dev

```bash
terraform init

terraform workspace new dev || terraform workspace select dev

export TF_VAR_db_password="$(aws secretsmanager get-secret-value \
  --secret-id webapp/dev/postgres-master-password \
  --query SecretString \
  --output text)"

terraform plan  -var-file=dev.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=dev.tfvars
```

### Prod

```bash
terraform workspace new prod || terraform workspace select prod

export TF_VAR_db_password="$(aws secretsmanager get-secret-value \
  --secret-id webapp/prod/postgres-master-password \
  --query SecretString \
  --output text)"

terraform plan  -var-file=prod.tfvars
terraform apply -var-file=prod.tfvars
```

The password is not committed to Git, but it will still be present as sensitive data in Terraform state. The remote state bucket therefore must have encryption, versioning, blocked public access, and tightly restricted IAM access.

This module covers the requested bucket, RDS instance, and service-account role. EKS node groups and HTTPS/CloudFront resources from the broader canonical scenario should be separate modules so their lifecycles remain independent.
